sec 7.4: a rogue succession of the root at seq 1, anchored by the key it names in the second of the genuine handing off at seq 2, lowers the retiring seq to 1; the genuine history at seq 1, reached only through the genuine succession's record of that second, sits at the retiring seq and is timely, a fork at 1 with the rogue; the genuine succession above the retiring seq admits nobody and the successor is EXCLUDED.
